\name{run_lisa_de}
\alias{run_lisa_de}
\title{Run one differential-expression analysis with LISA}
\usage{
run_lisa_de(input, output_dir, comparison_name = NULL,
  species = "Homo sapiens", symbol_col = NULL, rank_col = NULL,
  logfc_col = NULL, pvalue_col = NULL, padj_col = NULL,
  universes = lisa_default_collections(),
  lisa_dictionary = "core", term2gene_path = NULL,
  make_heatmaps = FALSE, ...,
  trusted_rds = FALSE, rds_max_bytes = 512 * 1024^2)
}
\arguments{
\item{input}{Differential-expression table path, data frame or supported object.}
\item{output_dir}{Directory in which to write the analysis.}
\item{comparison_name}{Portable ASCII technical identifier used in output
paths and file names. Human-readable Unicode belongs in a separate title or
label field.}
\item{species}{Species represented by the input identifiers.}
\item{symbol_col, rank_col, logfc_col, pvalue_col, padj_col}{Explicit input column names.}
\item{universes}{Gene-set collections to analyse. The five options are
\code{"GOBP-C2"}, \code{"GOMF"}, \code{"GOCC"}, \code{"PATHWAYS"} and
\code{"HALLMARKS"}.}
\item{lisa_dictionary}{Dictionary tier. \code{"core"} resolves the registered
  \code{lisa_dictionary_core@1.0.0} resource and \code{"expanded"} resolves
  \code{lisa_dictionary_expanded@1.0.0}. Both dictionaries are bundled with lisaR;
  the scientific TERM2GENE membership resource is obtained separately.}
\item{term2gene_path}{Optional species-matched TERM2GENE file.}
\item{make_heatmaps}{Reserved compatibility flag. In version 1.0 this
lower-level function warns and does not generate heatmaps. Use a configured
\code{run_lisa()} study with an expression matrix, then request the
\code{heatmap} product through \code{render_lisa_categories()}.}
\item{...}{Named advanced arguments passed to the single-analysis engine.
Every argument supplied through \code{...} must have an explicit name.
\code{category_nes_variants} selects a nonempty unique subset of
\code{c("clean", "percentages", "direction", "dispersion")}; all four are generated by
default when GSEA category plots are requested. The views share the same mean,
category order and axes. Direction adds the median and percentages among
significant member sets; dispersion additionally shows P25--P75 (type 7), not
a confidence interval. PNG, PDF and SVG are supported for these views.
Their source, settings and recipe are retained together. Direct HALLMARKS
views are not semantic categories and do not receive these variants.}
\item{trusted_rds}{Whether this local R call explicitly trusts a local,
stable and fully trusted \code{.rds} input. The default is \code{FALSE};
YAML/JSON configurations cannot enable it. Because it follows \code{...}, it
must be named explicitly. The file must remain under the caller's control and
must not be modified or replaced while it is checked and deserialized.}
\item{rds_max_bytes}{Maximum serialized-file and approximate in-memory object
size accepted when \code{trusted_rds = TRUE}. It is a diagnostic limit, not a
sandbox or a hard memory-safety boundary for hostile or extremely compressed
RDS files. Because it follows \code{...}, it must be named explicitly.}
}
\value{A list containing \code{comparison_name}, \code{output_dir}, ranking
QC, GSEA and ORA tables, category summaries, and trusted-input receipt details
when applicable.}
\description{Runs enrichment and semantic category analysis for one differential-expression result.}
\details{
Every accepted RDS produces a portable
\code{lisa_rds_input_receipt_v2} receipt. \code{source_sha256} identifies the
serialized file and \code{object_sha256} identifies the validated object using
R serialization version 3 in XDR form. The latter is an internal
branch-integrity fingerprint, not a stable semantic identity across R or
package versions. Absolute source paths are omitted from the receipt.
}
\examples{
# The installed sample data make this complete example offline. The
# calculation is left for an interactive session because it creates a full
# set of scientific tables and figures.
if (interactive()) {
  de_path <- system.file(
    "examples", "quick-start", "data", "de_a.tsv",
    package = "lisaR"
  )
  resource <- function(file) system.file(
    "extdata", "quick-start", file, package = "lisaR"
  )
  de_result <- run_lisa_de(
    input = de_path,
    output_dir = tempfile("lisa-de-example-"),
    comparison_name = "response_a",
    species = "Homo sapiens",
    symbol_col = "symbol",
    rank_col = "stat",
    logfc_col = "log2FoldChange",
    pvalue_col = "pvalue",
    padj_col = "padj",
    universes = "GOBP-C2",
    lisa_dictionary = "sample",
    term2gene_path = resource("example_term2gene_v2_1.tsv"),
    lisa_dictionary_path = resource("example_dictionary_v3_0.tsv"),
    category_map_path = resource("example_category_map_v1_1.tsv"),
    export_formats = "tsv",
    verbose = FALSE
  )
  de_result$output_dir
  names(de_result$summaries)
}
}
